1. Introduction to the WCST Nethack Newsletter
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
This is the first issue of the WCST Nethack Newsletter.  We've created it for
several reasons.  First, it will allow us to regularly give you small updates
to the Spoilers - particularly to correct errors.  Second, it will allow us
to keep you up to date on the progress of the next version of the Spoilers
and other things that we're working on.  Third, it will always contain one or
two articles that explain a particular aspect of the game, give background
information about the game, or in general give other interesting information
about Nethack.  At this point, I'm intending the WCST Nethack Newsletter to
be a monthly phenomenon, but that will (of course) depend on how often I can
get around to making the next issue.

We will be posting the WCST Nethack Newsletter to rec.games.hack for general
distribution.  However, I know that some of your news sites have rather quick
expiration times, some of you don't have easy access to news, and some of you
will just want your own private copy of the Newsletter anyways.  With that in
mind, I'm creating a WCST e-mailing list.  People on the WCST e-mailing list
will get the WCST Nethack Newsletter sent to them via e-mail, and (if my
system administrator will allow it - we'll have to wait and see) may get
private e-mail copies of future WCST releases of the Spoilers, etc.  If you'd
like to be on the WCST e-mailing list, just send me e-mail telling me that
you'd like to be on the list, and giving me the best address to get through
to you on.  I will acknowledge your request, so if you don't get anything
from me, send your info again.  E-mail addresses that you can get to me at
are listed at the bottom of this Newsletter, or you can probably just hit 'r'
to reply to this posting.

We also are always happy to get corrections, amplifications, or additions to
the Spoilers.  Also, please feel free to send us ideas for articles in future
issues of the WCST Nethack Newsletter or send us a fully written up article.
For that matter, even send us ideas in general for the Spoilers or the
Newsletter!  Don't, however, send us ideas about Nethack - we can't really do
anything about that, so send them to the Nethack Dev Team instead.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. WCST Nethack Spoiler Errata
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
This section is where we will inform you of any corrections that we may have
to the Spoilers.  In this issue we have just one, but I'm sure many more will
follow.

Under "General Hints" in the "Commonalities and Generalities" section, the
WCST Spoilers say that "A ring of levitation will protect you from a xan
(they're real short)."  This is false.  Levitating will not protect you from
being hit by a xan.  To protect against being hit by a xan, simply wear foot
armor (iron shoes, low boots, etc.) so that it can't prick you in the foot.

