4. Nethack Level Sizes and How to Find Vaults
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
The other day while I was watching my wife play Nethack, I learned something
very interesting.  She was looking for a vault on the level she was on (she
had heard someone counting money - a sure sign that a vault is on the level),
and I couldn't understand why she was digging where she was.  In an off-hand
manner (she assumed I knew this already) she told me "Nethack conserves
space, so I know the vault has to be over here."

Needless to say, I didn't understand what she meant, so I asked for an
amplification.  She gave me a look that sort of said "You mean you, the guru
of the Spoiler set, don't know this already?" and then proceeded to explain
it to me, gleefully rubbing her hands together at the thought that she knew
something which I didn't.  I found it so interesting that I decided to pass
it on to you.  Here's the basic picture...

Assume that you're on a level which looks like this:

        ---------                            -----------
        |.......|               ------       |.........|
        |.......+########       |....|       |.........|
        |.......|       #       |....|       |.........|
        -----|---       ###     |.....#######-.........|
             #            #     |....|       |.........|
             #            ######-....|       -----------
             #                  ----.-
         ----.---------           ###         ------------
         |............|           # #       ##-..........|
         |.............############ ######### |..........|
         --------------                       |..........|
                                              ------------

When Nethack generates a level, it stores information about a rectangular
area that only encompasses what is actually on the level.  In other words, if
this were all that were on the level, Nethack would only store a rectangle
big enough to represent just what you see.  If you were to dig off what is
mapped in any direction (i.e. beyond the northernmost, easternmost,
southernmost, or westernmost wall), you would be told "That wall is too hard
to dig into," even though there's still plenty of room on the screen.
Nethack isn't storing any information about that area, so it obviously can't
allow you to dig there!

So, let's draw that level again, only this time showing the undiggable areas
(represented as X's), and assuming that there's a vault on the level.  If you
try to dig into any spot represented by an 'X,' the game will tell you "That
wall is too hard to dig into."

XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX
XX      ---------                            -----------  XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX
XX      |.......|               ------       |.........|  XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX
XX      |.......+########       |....|       |.........|  XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX
XX      |.......|       #       |....|       |.........|  XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX
XX      -----|---       ###     |.....#######-.........|  XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX
XX           #            #     |....|       |.........|  XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX
XX           #            ######-....|       -----------  XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX
XX           #                  ----.-                    XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX
XX       ----.---------           ###         ------------XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX
XX       |............|           # #       ##-..........|XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX
XX       |.............############ ######### |..........|XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX
XX       --------------                       |..........|XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX
XX                                            ------------XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX
XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX

Most people, if they knew there was a vault on this level, wouldn't bother to
go looking for it (assuming they had a pick-axe).  They would look at the
large amount of open space on the right hand side of the screen, assume that
the vault must be somewhere in there, and decide that it would be far too
much trouble to dig out large sections of that area just to find a vault.

A couple of simple attempts to dig to the right, though, will quickly reveal
that Nethack isn't storing any information about that area.  Thus, the vault
can't be in that area.  This narrows down the area where the vault can be
considerably - obviously it's on the left hand side of the screen.  A few
experimental digs, and you can quickly find the hidden vault:

XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX
XX      ---------                            -----------  XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX
XX      |.......|               ------       |.........|  XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX
XX      |.......+########       |....|       |.........|  XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX
XX   ####.......|       #       |....|       |.........|  XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX
XX   #  -----|---       ###     |.....#######-.........|  XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX
XX   #       #            #     |....|       |.........|  XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX
XX   #       #            ######-....|       -----------  XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX
XX---#       #                  ----.-                    XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX
XX|$$#   ----.---------           ###         ------------XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX
XX|$$|   |............|           # #       ##-..........|XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX
XX----   |.............############ ######### |..........|XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX
XX       --------------                       |..........|XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX
XX                                            ------------XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX
XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX

You'll notice that I carefully chose the way in which I dug, such that I
would be sure to get the vault, no matter where it could be in that area, and
now that I've found the hidden vault, my character can load up with its gold
(always good for shops, temples, and extra points).

I hope this provides you with some useful information, and good luck at
finding your next vault!

