5. Carrying Infinite Weight with the Bag of Holding Bug
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
"What's the bag of holding trick?"  This is one of the more common questions
posted on rec.games.hack, and it rarely has gotten a definitive answer.
Quite simply stated, there is currently a bug in the bag of holding code
(although this bug has been fixed in the not yet released version 3.1) that
causes the game to not properly update weight when a bag of holding
containing items changes its blessed or cursed status.

By putting items into a bag of holding, cursing it, and then taking the items
out, you can quickly get to the point where you can carry virtually infinite
amounts of items.  Here's step-by-step instructions on how to do it:

A. First, you will need to get hold of several items.  Obviously, you will
   need a bag of holding.  You will also need three or four potions of holy
   water and three or four potions of unholy water.  Potions of holy water
   can be made by dropping water on a lawful altar, and likewise, potions of
   unholy water can be made by dropping water on a chaotic altar.

B. Next, make sure you have a large pile of worthless items.  For my pile of
   worthless items I used a large pile of rocks (about 3,000).  I acquired
   them by allowing rock moles and dwarves to completely dig out about three
   levels.  I then went around and picked up all of the rocks, and used a
   pick-axe to render all of the boulders down to rocks, and spent a long
   time moving all of the rocks into one pile.  This is probably the most
   tedious part of the job, but it's definitely worthwhile, because later on
   you can polymorph these rocks into gems to get mega points when you win
   the game.

C. Now then, drop everything except your bag of holding and one potion each
   of holy and unholy water.

D. Next, pick up all of the rocks that you can, and then stuff them into the
   bag of holding.  Now pick up as many more rocks as you can (you should be
   able to pick up about half as many rocks as the first time), and put them
   into the bag of holding.  Continue picking up rocks and stuffing them into
   the bag of holding until you can't stuff any more rocks into the bag.

E. Now, #dip the bag of holding into your potion of unholy water.  This will
   curse the bag of holding (incidentally, in a cursed bag of holding, some
   of the items may randomly disappear, so you may lose some of your rocks).

F. Take all of the rocks that are in the bag of holding out (you'll notice,
   interestingly enough, that you will now be able to carry all of the rocks
   you stuffed into the bag, even though you couldn't originally carry that
   many).

G. Then, #dip the bag of holding into your potion of holy water.  This will
   uncurse the bag.  You now have a far greater carrying capacity then
   before.  If you like, pick up another potion each of holy and unholy
   water, and go to step D.  Repeat this as many times as you like in order
   to allow you to pick up virtually infinite weights.

Two notes as regards using the above process:

First, in a Nethack game that I modified to show percent of maximum weight
being carried, after using this trick just three times, my character was
carrying -3000% of maximum weight allowed.  Needless to say, this meant that
he could pick up a *lot* of stuff and not be hampered by weight issues.

Second, if you repeat this trick more than twice, you will probably notice
that you cannot hit any monsters any more (not even easy to hit rats and
such with nasty named weapons and nasty bonuses).  This is because the game
figures into the to-hit probability what percentage of your maximum weight
you're currently carrying.  When this goes negative, as it does when you use
this trick, it can really throw the to-hit computation off.  The solution to
this problem is to pick up rocks or other dead weight until you can hit
monsters again.  You'll still be able to pick up a tons of stuff, and if you
need to, you can always put some of it into the bag of holding, which will
reduce those items' weight by half.

Good luck with this trick, although do remember that it won't be available in
the next version of Nethack!  You'll just have to play fair when version 3.1
comes out (although it will probably have its own bugs to take advantage of).

